Sam (CS): Hey team — customer reached out: their rerank call started returning 400 with "invalid input" and also weird scores (all zeros) after a change in their ingestion. They pasted payload. Can we triage?
Priya (DevEx): Can you drop the payload and the exact error body + request id?
Sam (CS): Error body: {
  "error": "invalid input",
  "code": "RERANK_SCHEMA_ERROR",
  "request_id": "req_05b3f9"
}
Payload (redacted customer sent):
```json
{
  "query": "how to reset password",
  "documents": [
    {
      "id": "doc-1",
      "passages": [
        {"text": "step 1"},
        {"text": "step 2"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "doc-2",
      "passages": [ {"text": "reset token"} ] }
  ]
}
```
Sam (CS): They said this used to work before, then they added a small transform that nested the snippets into passages.
Marta (Eng-ML): This is exactly the mismatch. Rerank expects a flat list under `candidates` or `documents` depending on API version, but each candidate must have a top-level `text` (or `content`) field for the model scoring. We don't traverse `passages` unless they use the multi-passages flag.
Priya (DevEx): Which flag is that? I thought we auto-detect passages arrays.
Marta (Eng-ML): We don't auto-flatten nested `passages`. Current v1 rerank schema: top-level key `candidates`: [ {"id":..., "text":...} ] OR `documents`: [ {"id":..., "text":...} ]. If customers want per-document passages they must set `passage_mode": true` and provide `passages` array where each passage has `text`. Otherwise the server treats the candidate as missing the text and returns a schema error or fallback zero score.
Ben (Platform): @Marta can you paste the minimal repro we can use to validate? I'll add a quick ingestion rule to detect this pattern and warn in the console.
Marta (Eng-ML): Minimal repro — two variants:
1) Failing payload (what customer sent):
```json
{
  "query": "how to reset password",
  "documents": [
    {"id":"d1","passages":[{"text":"step1"}] }
  ]
}
```
2) Working payload (flattened):
```json
{
  "query": "how to reset password",
  "candidates": [
    {"id":"d1","text":"step1"}
  ]
}
```
Marta (Eng-ML): Or, if they want passage-level scoring: add `passage_mode: true` and use `documents` with `passages`. Example:
```json
{
  "query":"how to reset password",
  "passage_mode": true,
  "documents": [
    {"id":"d1","passages":[{"text":"step1"},{"text":"step2"}]}
  ]
}
```
Priya (DevEx): Nice. Also there's been confusion around `query` vs `q` — our SDK accepts both but the raw API requires `query`. Customer used `q` earlier and our middleware used to translate it; that translation was removed in a patch last month. Might explain why they say it "used to work".
Sam (CS): They did use `q` in the older payload in their ticket thread, yes. They updated transform to nest passages and kept `q`. So double mismatch.
Marta (Eng-ML): That can lead to two failure modes: missing query (we return 400) or missing candidate text (we return schema error or zero scores). Also watch for limits — we enforce max candidates = 200 and max passages per doc = 20. If nested arrays push us over, we currently error with 413-like body.
Ben (Platform): Action items: (1) I'll add a console warning for payloads that contain `documents[*].passages` without `passage_mode` and no flattening, (2) add a note in the API logs to surface `q`->`query` translation removal, (3) run a quick auto-fix script suggestion in the support UI.
Priya (DevEx): For support reply: give them quick repro (working v failing), ask them to send request_id (req_05b3f9) + raw body. Offer temporary workaround script to flatten passages into candidates.
Sam (CS): I'll reply now with repro snippets and request id.
rerank-bot: Ticket #INC-4829 created for follow-up. Assigned to Marta and Ben. ETA 48h. :spiral_calendar:
Marta (Eng-ML): I'll own the diagnostic and patch the docs to be explicit about `passage_mode` and `query` names. Also adding a regression test for nested `passages` returning zero scores.
Ben (Platform): I'll push the console warning PR and include telemetry to count occurrences.
Priya (DevEx): I'll update the SDK changelog + add a short note in quickstarts.
Sam (CS): Thanks all — I'll mark this as escalated to priority P2 and update the customer once we have the fix or a clear workaround.
